INSERT INTO article (id, slug, path, section, title, h1, meta_description, body_md, word_count, reading_minutes, author, featured_image_id, published_at, modified_at, schema_disabled, is_published) VALUES (11, '5-quick-and-easy-south-indian-one-pot-rice-recipes', 'recipe/5-quick-and-easy-south-indian-one-pot-rice-recipes', 'recipe', '5 Quick and Easy South Indian One-Pot Rice Recipes', '5 Quick and Easy One-Pot Rice Recipes in South Indian', 'Discover the rich flavors of South Indian One-Pot Rice Recipes. Simplify your cooking routine while savoring traditional tastes.', 'Explore South Indian cuisine with these five quick one-pot rice recipes, from traditional Biryani to comforting Lemon Rice. Let’s embark on a spice-filled culinary journey together!

## 1. Vegetable Biryani

![Vegetable Biryani](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Vegetable-Biryani.webp)

Experience the delightful combination of fragrant basmati rice, mixed vegetables, and aromatic spices in this Vegetable Biryani. A classic South Indian dish, this one-pot wonder is both flavorful and satisfying.

**Ingredients:**

- Basmati rice

- Mixed vegetables (carrots, peas, potatoes)

- Onion, sliced

- Tomato, chopped

- Ginger-garlic paste

- Biryani masala

- Ghee

- Cashews

- Fresh coriander leaves

- Mint leaves

- Salt to taste
**Instructions:**

- Sauté sliced onions until golden in ghee.

- Add ginger-garlic paste and chopped tomatoes; cook until soft.

- Mix in biryani masala and sauté.

- Add mixed vegetables, rice, and water.

- Cook until the rice is tender and garnish with cashews, coriander, and mint leaves.
Continue reading for more one-pot rice recipes inspiration!

## 2. Lemon Rice

![Lemon Rice](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Lemon-Rice.webp)

Bring a burst of citrusy freshness to your table with Lemon Rice. This quick and easy dish is a staple in South Indian households, offering a zesty twist to plain rice.

**Ingredients:**

- Cooked rice

- Mustard seeds

- Urad dal

- Chana dal

- Peanuts

- Curry leaves

- Green chilies, chopped

- Turmeric powder

- Lemon juice

- Salt to taste
**Instructions:**

- In hot oil, temper mustard seeds, urad dal, and chana dal.

- Add peanuts, curry leaves, and chopped green chilies.

- Mix in turmeric powder and sauté.

- Add cooked rice, lemon juice, and salt; stir until well combined.

## 3. Tomato Rice (Thakkali Sadam)

![Tomato Rice](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Tomato-Rice.webp)

Indulge in the tangy goodness of Tomato Rice, known as Thakkali Sadam in South India. This flavorful dish is a delightful blend of ripe tomatoes, aromatic spices, and perfectly cooked rice.

**Ingredients:**

- Cooked rice

- Ripe tomatoes, chopped

- Mustard seeds

- Urad dal

- Chana dal

- Curry leaves

- Green chilies, chopped

- Ginger, grated

- Turmeric powder

- Asafoetida (hing)

- Coriander leaves for garnish

- Salt to taste
**Instructions:**

- In hot oil, temper mustard seeds, urad dal, and chana dal.

- Add chopped tomatoes, grated ginger, and chopped green chilies.

- Stir in turmeric powder and a pinch of asafoetida.

- Cook until tomatoes are soft, then add cooked rice and salt.

- Garnish with fresh coriander leaves before serving.

## 4. Coconut Milk Pulao

![Coconut Milk Pulao](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Coconut-Milk-Pulao.webp)

Transport your taste buds to the coastal regions of South India with Coconut Milk Pulao. This rich and creamy one-pot dish combines fragrant rice with coconut milk, creating a symphony of flavours.

**Ingredients:**

- Cooked rice

- Ripe tomatoes, chopped

- Mustard seeds

- Urad dal

- Chana dal

- Curry leaves

- Green chilies, chopped

- Ginger, grated

- Turmeric powder

- Asafoetida (hing)

- Coriander leaves for garnish

- Salt to taste
**Instructions:**

- In hot oil, temper mustard seeds, urad dal, and chana dal.

- Add chopped tomatoes, grated ginger, and chopped green chilies.

- Stir in turmeric powder and a pinch of asafoetida.

- Cook until tomatoes are soft, then add cooked rice and salt.

- Garnish with fresh coriander leaves before serving.

## 5. Tamarind Rice (Puliyodarai)

![Tamarind Rice](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Tamarind-Rice.webp)

Enjoy the unique and tangy flavor of Tamarind Rice, or Puliyodarai, a South Indian favorite. This quick and easy one-pot meal combines the sourness of tamarind with a medley of spices, creating a delightful dish.

**Ingredients:**

- Cooked rice

- Tamarind pulp

- Mustard seeds

- Urad dal

- Chana dal

- Peanuts

- Curry leaves

- Red chili powder

- Turmeric powder

- Asafoetida (hing)

- Jaggery

- Gingelly oil

- Salt to taste
**Instructions:**

- In hot oil, temper mustard seeds, urad dal, and chana dal.

- Add peanuts, curry leaves, and a pinch of asafoetida.

- Mix in tamarind pulp, red chili powder, and turmeric powder.

- Add jaggery and salt; cook until the mixture thickens.

- Combine with cooked rice, drizzle with gingelly oil, and mix well.

## Final thoughts

Discover eight quick one-pot rice recipes with vibrant South Indian flavours, from aromatic Vegetable Biryani to zesty Lemon Rice and tangy Tamarind Rice. Simplify your South Indian cooking with VATTI appliances – elevating your culinary experience effortlessly!

