INSERT INTO article (id, slug, path, section, title, h1, meta_description, body_md, word_count, reading_minutes, author, featured_image_id, published_at, modified_at, schema_disabled, is_published) VALUES (16, '5-best-asian-soup-recipes', 'recipe/5-best-asian-soup-recipes', 'recipe', '5 Best Asian Soup Recipes to Warm Your Soul', '5 best Asian Soup Recipes to Warm Your Soul', 'Warm your soul with 5 best Asian Soup Recipes, a delightful collection of comforting soups to satisfy your cravings.', 'Embark on a delightful journey with these five best Asian soup recipes, promising a comforting experience that transports you to the heart of Asia. From rich broths to aromatic spices, these recipes are crafted to warm your soul and tantalize your taste buds.

## Before we get started

Find the perfect cooker hob to suit your cooking style.

[Check it out here](/cooker-hob-in-malaysia/)

## 1. Miso Ramen with Vegetables

![Miso Ramen with Vegetables](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Miso-Ramen-with-Vegetables.webp)

Begin your Asian soup adventure with Miso Ramen, a soul-warming bowl featuring a savory miso broth, chewy ramen noodles, and a medley of fresh vegetables. This quick and satisfying recipe captures the essence of Japanese comfort food.

**Ingredients:**

- Ramen noodles

- Miso paste

- Vegetable broth

- Tofu, cubed

- Mushrooms, sliced

- Bok choy, chopped

- Green onions, sliced

- Sesame oil
**Instructions:**

- Cook ramen noodles according to package instructions.

- In a pot, combine vegetable broth and miso paste, bringing it to a gentle simmer.

- Add tofu, mushrooms, and bok choy, cooking until vegetables are tender.

- Pour the miso broth over cooked ramen noodles.

- Garnish with green onions and a drizzle of sesame oil.
Continue reading for more soul-warming Asian soup recipes!

## 2. Tom Yum Soup with Shrimp

![Tom Yum Soup with Shrimp](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Tom-Yum-Soup-with-Shrimp.webp)

Transport your taste buds to Thailand with Tom Yum Soup, a zesty and aromatic broth featuring succulent shrimp, fragrant lemongrass, and a kick of chili heat. This Thai classic is perfect for those craving a flavourful and invigorating soup.

**Ingredients:**

- Shrimp, peeled and deveined

- Tomatoes, diced

- Mushrooms, sliced

- Lemongrass, crushed

- Thai bird chilies, sliced

- Lime juice

- Fish sauce

- Fresh cilantro, chopped
**Instructions:**

- In a pot, bring water to a boil and add lemongrass, Thai bird chilies, and fish sauce.

- Add shrimp, mushrooms, and tomatoes, simmering until shrimp turn pink.

- Finish with a squeeze of lime juice and fresh cilantro.

- Serve hot and enjoy the bold flavours of Tom Yum Soup.
**RELATED:**[5 Quick and Easy Rice Cooking Wine Recipes](/recipe/5-delicous-and-easy-rice-cooker-recipes-for-every-meal/)

## 3. Korean Kimchi Jjigae

![Korean Kimchi Jjigae](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Korean-Kimchi-Jjigae.webp)

Experience the heartiness of Korean cuisine with Kimchi Jjigae, a robust stew featuring fermented kimchi, pork, and tofu. Packed with umami and a touch of spiciness, this Korean classic is a comforting delight.

**Ingredients:**

- Kimchi, chopped

- Pork belly, sliced

- Tofu, cubed

- Onion, sliced

- Garlic, minced

- Gochugaru (Korean red pepper flakes)

- Soy sauce

- Sesame oil
**Instructions:**

- Sauté pork belly in sesame oil until browned.

- Add garlic, sliced onion, and gochugaru, stirring until fragrant.

- Incorporate chopped kimchi, tofu, and soy sauce, allowing the flavors to meld.

- Pour in water and simmer until the stew reaches a rich consistency.

- Serve hot, savoring the hearty warmth of Kimchi Jjigae.

## 4. Chinese Hot and Sour Soup

![Chinese Hot and Sour Soup](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Chinese-Hot-and-Sour-Soup.webp)

Delight in the contrasting flavours of Chinese Hot and Sour Soup, a tantalizing blend of spicy and tangy notes. Loaded with tofu, mushrooms, and bamboo shoots, this soup offers a symphony of tastes that will invigorate your senses.

**Ingredients:**

- Tofu, cubed

- Mushrooms, sliced

- Bamboo shoots, julienned

- Eggs, beaten

- Chicken or vegetable broth

- Soy sauce

- Rice vinegar

- Sesame oil
**Instructions:**

- Bring broth to a simmer and add tofu, mushrooms, and bamboo shoots.

- Drizzle in beaten eggs, stirring gently to create silky ribbons.

- Season with soy sauce, rice vinegar, and sesame oil.

- Simmer until ingredients are well-infused.

- Serve piping hot and relish the bold flavors of Chinese Hot and Sour Soup.
**RELATED:**[5 Quick and Easy One-Pot Rice Recipes in South Indian](/recipe/5-quick-and-easy-south-indian-one-pot-rice-recipes/)

## 5. Vietnamese Pho Bo

![Vietnamese Pho Bo](https://pub-d0b729df0b8f422289c6f46d17d33f3e.r2.dev/2024/01/Vietnamese-Pho-Bo.webp)

Conclude your culinary journey with Vietnamese Pho Bo, a fragrant and soul-soothing noodle soup. This iconic dish features aromatic spices, thinly sliced beef, and fresh herbs, creating a harmonious bowl of warmth that’s synonymous with Vietnamese comfort.

**Ingredients:**

- Rice noodles

- Beef sirloin, thinly sliced

- Beef broth

- Star anise, cinnamon, cloves

- Bean sprouts, basil, lime, chili

- Hoisin sauce, Sriracha
**Instructions:**

- Cook rice noodles according to package instructions.

- In a pot, simmer beef broth with star anise, cinnamon, and cloves.

- Arrange rice noodles and thinly sliced beef in bowls.

- Ladle hot broth over the noodles and beef, allowing it to cook the meat.

- Serve with a side of fresh bean sprouts, basil, lime, chili, hoisin sauce, and Sriracha.

## Final thoughts

Discover five delicious Asian soup recipes from Miso Ramen to Vietnamese Pho Bo that will warm your soul. Ready to enhance your soup-making? Explore VATTI appliances for an even more enjoyable Asian culinary experience!

